# Build-context DENY-LIST for every repo-root build: every compose service with
# `context: ..` (all of them except smart-exporter, which builds from deploy/smart-exporter).
# BuildKit sends only the paths a Dockerfile COPYs, so this file is defence in depth: it
# keeps secrets, scratch and toolchain output out of any COPY that names a whole tree. A new
# app or COPY path needs no line here.
#
# ⚠ Keep it a pure deny-list: no `!` re-includes. A wildcard re-include stops the BuildKit
# client from pruning excluded directories, so it walks all of them (.git, .claude/worktrees,
# every node_modules) and fails on any it cannot read. The old allowlist (0037 OPS-1) had to
# stay literal for that reason; it existed because the deny-list before it let
# dagster/Dockerfile bake ~23 GB of in-tree runtime data. That data now lives under the data
# root (config.kdl data.root), outside every checkout, and the published datasets live in
# astra-data, so neither can enter an image.

# --- Never a build input: VCS, agent worktrees, developer scratch, docs, host tooling. ---
.git
.claude
.claude-plugin
.github
.githooks
.playwright-mcp
artifacts
thoughts
docs
sheets
scripts
fixtures
# deploy/ holds the SOPS file and possibly age.key; smart-exporter builds from its own
# context, so no repo-root build reads deploy/.
deploy

# --- Secrets anywhere else. ---
**/.env
**/.env.*
**/*.agekey
**/age.key

# --- Toolchain output and caches: rebuilt in-image (node_modules by pnpm install, the venv
# by uv sync, dist/ by the app build) or irrelevant to any build. ---
**/node_modules
**/.venv
**/dist
**/.output
**/.nitro
**/.tanstack
**/.tsbuild
**/storybook-static
**/target
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.pytest_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.ty_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.DS_Store

# --- Regenerated by each frontend's own build (build-content in the vite buildStart hook),
# so a host copy is stale by definition. ---
apps/*/*/src/generated/*
apps/akasha/web/public/static
apps/akasha/web/public/index.xml
apps/akasha/web/public/sitemap.xml
apps/mouthpiece/web/public/episodes.json

# --- Host-only material inside source trees: codex's book sources and art (37 MB; no build
# reads them), codex's fixture corpus (tests only; a built server never serves it, it fails
# closed without the real corpus) and assay's output. ---
apps/codex/web/books
apps/codex/web/fixtures
apps/assay/py/out
